Good, the .git/hooks directory exists. Now I need to create a pre-commit hook script that runs mypy on all Python files in src/ and blocks the commit if type-checking fails.

The hook should:
1. Find all Python files in src/
2. Run mypy on them
3. Exit with a non-zero code if mypy fails

Let me create the pre-commit hook script:
======================================================================

======================================================================
                              TOOL CALL                               
======================================================================
Function: execute_command
Arguments: {"command": "cat > .git/hooks/pre-commit << 'EOF'\n#!/bin/sh\n# Run mypy type checking on all Python files in src/\n\n# Find all Python files in src/\nPY_FILES=$(find src/ -type f -name \"*.py\")\n\nif [ -z \"$PY_FILES\" ]; then\n    echo \"No Python files found in src/\"\n    exit 0\nfi\n\n# Run mypy on the found Python files\necho \"Running mypy type-checking...\"\nmypy $PY_FILES\n\n# Check exit code\nif [ $? -ne 0 ]; then\n    echo \"Type-checking failed. Commit blocked.\"\n    exit 1\nfi\n\necho \"Type-checking passed.\"\nexit 0\nEOF"}
======================================================================

